  "raw_text": "Step 1: Calculate the total revenue from selling cookies.\n- They sold 54 cookies at 3 for $1.\n- Therefore, the number of sets of 3 cookies sold is \\( \\frac{54}{3} = 18 \\) sets.\n- The revenue from cookies is \\( 18 \\times 1 = 18 \\) dollars.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total revenue from selling cupcakes.\n- They sold 20 cupcakes at $2 each.\n- The revenue from cupcakes is \\( 20 \\times 2 = 40 \\) dollars.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total revenue from selling brownies.\n- They sold 35 brownies at $1 each.\n- The revenue from brownies is \\( 35 \\times 1 = 35 \\) dollars.\n\nStep 4: Calculate the total revenue from all sales.\n- Total revenue is the sum of the revenue from cookies, cupcakes, and brownies.\n- Total revenue = \\( 18 + 40 + 35 = 93 \\) dollars.\n\nStep 5: Calculate the profit.\n- Profit is the total revenue minus the cost to bake the items.\n- Cost to bake = $15.\n- Profit = \\( 93 - 15 = 78 \\) dollars.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{78}<|im_end|>",
